OP_REGION_TO_POOL zeroes the whole range again, work in its size,
and does not say so where it calls memset,
so a walk the table of "Bounded work" no longer lists hides behind a call.
Each object is still zeroed as it is allocated, so only the loop check catches it.

Caught-by: loop-bounds

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
index 90f522a..52d38be 100644
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -152,2 +152,3 @@ static int op_region(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
          */
+        memset(p2v(base), 0, size);
         struct pool *pool = pool_create(base, size, cap->rights, obj_pool(&t->hdr));
